public static int calculateUniqueSum(int[] nums) {
    Set<Integer> uniqueElements = new HashSet<>();
    int sum = 0;
    for (int num : nums) {
        uniqueElements.add(num);
        sum += num;
    }
    return sum - uniqueElements.size() * uniqueElements.stream().findFirst().get();
}
```
This Java method calculates the sum of unique elements in an array by first adding each element to a `HashSet`. Since a set automatically removes duplicates, only unique elements are stored. It then calculates the total sum by adding the total number of elements to the sum of these unique elements. The sum is then adjusted by subtracting the size of the set multiplied by the smallest possible value in the set (which is unrepresented by a negative number) to exclude duplicates from the sum.

